f Production \\nResearch, vol. 60, no. 18, pp. 5675-5696, 2022. \\n[31] D. Guo, R. Y. Zhong, P. Lin, Z. Lyu, Y. Rong, and G. Q. Huang, \\n\\\"Digital twin-enabled Graduation Intelligent Manufacturing \\nSystem for fixed-position assembly islands,\\\" Robotics and \\nComputer-Integrated Manufacturing, vol. 63, pp. 101917, 2020. \\n \\nAUTHOR BIOGRAPHIES \\nMingxing Li (Member, IEEE) received the B.Eng. \\ndegree from Tongji University, Shanghai, China, in \\n2018, and the Ph.D. degree in industrial and \\nmanufacturing systems engineering from The \\nUniversity of Hong Kong, Hong Kong, China, in 2022. \\nHe is currently an Associate Professor with the \\nSchool of Intelligent Systems Science and Engineering, \\nJinan University. His research area includes production \\nand intralogistics operations management, real-time data-driven decision-\\nmaking, and Industry 4.0 manufacturing. One of his papers has been \\nselected as ESI Top 1% highly cited paper in engineering. He has received \\nthe 2023 IJPR Top Trending Article award and best/outstanding paper \\nawards of several conferences. \\n \\nTing Qu (Senior Member, IEEE) received the B.Eng. \\nand M.Phil. degrees in Mechanical Engineering from \\nXi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, China, and the Ph.D. \\ndegree in Industrial and Manufacturing Systems \\nEngineering from The University of Hong Kong, Hong \\nKong, China. \\nHe is currently a Professor with the School of \\nIntelligent Systems Science and Engineering, Jinan \\nUniversity. His research interests include smart manufacturing systems, \\nlogistics and supply chain management, and industrial product/production \\nservice systems. He has undertaken over twenty research projects funded \\nby government and industry and has published nearly 200 technical papers. \\nHe serves as the Director or Board Member of several academic \\nassociations in industrial engineering and smart manufacturing areas. \\n \\nBinyang Liu received the B.E. degree in Logistics \\nEngineering from Xihua University in 2023. She is \\ncurrently pursuing the M.E. degree in Logistics \\nEngineering and Management at Jinan University. Her \\nresearch interests include the operational control of \\nintelligent manufacturing systems and synchronized \\nproduction-logistics decision-making and control. \\n \\n \\n  \\nQijie Luo received the B.S. degree in Industrial \\nEngineering from Jinan University, Zhuhai, Guangdong, \\nChina, in 2024. She is currently pursuing the M.S. \\ndegree. Her research interests include intelligent \\nmanufacturing systems, smart logistics, and production-\\nlogistics collaborative scheduling. \\n \\n \\n \\nMian Yan received the Ph.D. degree in industrial and \\nmanufacturing systems engineering from The \\nUniversity of Hong Kong, Hong Kong, China. \\nHe is currently an Associate Professor with the \\nSchool of Intelligent Systems Science and Engineering, \\nJinan University. His research interests include human \\nfactors engineering, ergonomics, technology acceptance \\nand implementation methods. His research has appeared \\nin International Journal of Industrial Ergonomics, Computers and \\nIndustrial Engineering, Transportation Research Part A, Transportation \\nResearch Part F, International Journal of Disaster Risk Reduction, \\nInternational Journal of Production Economics, and others. \\n \\nMing Li (Senior Member, IEEE) received the dual \\nbachelor's degrees in computer science and finance \\nfrom the South China University of Technology, \\nGuangzhou, China, in 2012, the M.S. degree in \\nindustrial engineering and logistics management in \\n2013, and the Ph.D. degree in industrial engineering \\nfrom the Department of Industrial and Manufacturing \\nSystems Engineering, The University of Hong Kong, \\nHong Kong, China, in 2018. \\nHe is currently a Research Assistant Professor with the Department of \\nIndustrial and Systems Engineering, The Hong Kong Polytechnic \\nUniversity, Hong Kong, China. His research